mb-framepacing licenses
=======================

Copyright (c) 2026, Mana Battery ApS

This repository is licensed under two licenses, by path:

- The BSD 3-Clause License (Part 1 below) covers everything under sdk/: the frame marker code that applications embed, the
  marker format, and the libraries and formats of the data the tools write:
  - sdk/cpp/, sdk/csharp/, sdk/python/, sdk/unity/ and sdk/shaders/ (the SDK's libraries in every language: the frame marker, and
    reading and writing the capture data and the analysis output)
  - sdk/doc/ (the marker format specification, the guides to integrating the markers, filling their fields and the Unity
    package, the vocabulary, and the data formats)
  - sdk/test-data/ (the golden marker images and the data libraries' golden data)
  sdk/LICENSE holds the BSD 3-Clause License on its own.

- The PolyForm Perimeter License 1.0.1 (Part 2 below) covers everything else: the measurement tools and their
  libraries, the scripts, the other documentation, and the build and CI files.

Every source file names its license on an SPDX-License-Identifier line near its top, and every code file
names its copyright holder on an SPDX-FileCopyrightText line right before it (SPDX file tags, ISO/IEC 5962):

    SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (C) 2026 Mana Battery ApS
    SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause

- BSD-3-Clause: the BSD 3-Clause License (Part 1).
- LicenseRef-PolyForm-Perimeter-1.0.1: the PolyForm Perimeter License 1.0.1 (Part 2). It is not on the SPDX
  license list, so its identifier starts with LicenseRef-.

Files without such a line (documentation, data, images) are covered by the paths above.

Third-party components keep their own licenses; see licenses/README.md.

